  "question": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>28</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn></math> L of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is produced on complete combustion of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> gaseous mixture of ethene and methane at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> atm. Heat evolved during the combustion process is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi></math></p><p>Given<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mfenced><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#916;H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p>",
